@@ -128,6 +128,34 @@ A packed Mac app exposes `DM_MIC` in its settings list when a game imports the s
 
 The Mac launcher stores a selected input device's Core Audio UID as the string `launcher.DM_MIC_DEVICE` in the app's preferences. A `DM_MIC_DEVICE` set at launch or in an env file takes precedence. Use `default` to follow the system input. `DM_MIC_GAIN` uses the saved choices described above.
 
+## Streaming front ends
+
+A front end that shows the game somewhere else (another device) starts the host with `DM_STREAM=<path of a Unix socket it listens on>`. The host runs with no window, no sound device and no microphone (`DM_MIC` is forced off: the packed app asks for no access, and the host opens no input device), connects to the socket, and from then on the front end is the picture, the sound and the controllers.
+
+Messages in both directions: `u32` length of (type + payload), `u8` type, payload. Integers are little-endian and fields are packed in the order below; floats are IEEE-754 bits. A length of 0 or above 8 MiB ends the stream. Version: `STREAM_TAP_VERSION` in `dm/host/stream.h`; a layout change bumps it on both sides.
+
+| Type | Name | From | Fields (bytes) |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 0x01 | hello | host | version 2 (2), title ID 16 (ASCII, `0x00` padded), name length 2, name (UTF-8) |
+| 0x02 | video | host | frame 4 (from 0; a gap is a frame dropped after encoding), capture ns 8, width 2, height 2, flags 1 (bit 0 = key frame; bit 1 = repair frame: encoded with ForceLTRRefresh and not a key frame; a key frame is never also a repair frame; other bits 0), token 4 (signed: the frame's long-term reference token, opaque, -1 for none), data: 4-byte big-endian length-prefixed HEVC NAL units, a key frame led by VPS, SPS, PPS |
+| 0x03 | audio | host | capture ns 8, channels 1 (2), 48 kHz 16-bit PCM, 240 frames (5 ms) |
+| 0x04 | prepare | host | phase 1 (1 the prewarm lists' pipelines, 2 the shader pairs' prebuild; other values may come), done 4, total 4: the prepare step before the first frame |
+| 0x10 | config | front end | max width 2, max height 2, max fps 1, bitrate 4 (bit/s); video starts with the first one |
+| 0x11 | keyframe | front end | none: the next frame is a key frame |
+| 0x12 | pad | front end | player 1 (0 to 7), buttons 8 (`DM_BTN_*`), lx 4, ly 4, rx 4, ry 4 (signed) |
+| 0x13 | motion | front end | player 1, frame 1 (0 controller, 1 the phone's, player 0 only), acceleration 3 x 4 (G), rotation 3 x 4 (rad/s) |
+| 0x14 | players | front end | mask 4 (bit p: player p + 1 has a controller) |
+| 0x15 | pause | front end | on 1: the background sequence (as `DM_OE_SCRIPT` `bg=1` / `bg=0`); a repeat of the current state is ignored |
+| 0x16 | quit | front end | none: a graceful exit (as SIGTERM) |
+| 0x17 | motionClear | front end | player 1 |
+| 0x18 | ltrAck | front end | count 1 (1 to 16), count x token 4 (signed): the front end decoded the frames that carried these tokens, each returned unchanged |
+| 0x19 | refresh | front end | none: a frame was lost; the next frame depends on nothing the front end may not have |
+
+- Sound: each silent sound output pushes a 5 ms block; the first to push is the clock, and each of its pushes sends one message mixing its block with the latest queued block of every other output (a 6-channel output without a stereo fold is mixed at 0.7071, the sum saturates). An output silent for 100 ms is forgotten.
+- Long-term references: a frame that carries a token (not every frame does; once the front end acknowledges tokens, each next frame does) can be acknowledged with `ltrAck` when the front end has decoded it. After a `refresh` the next frame is predicted only from an acknowledged frame, or is a key frame when nothing was acknowledged since the last key frame. A token is opaque: the front end returns it exactly as the video message carried it (it holds the encoder session, so an acknowledgement from before a size change never counts in the new one). Only tokens issued since the last key frame of the current session count; others, and repeats, are ignored. A refresh that arrives while the key frame or refresh that serves an earlier one is still being encoded is served by that frame. A non-key frame cannot be told from an ordinary one by its content, and ordinary frames encoded before the refresh was read can still be in flight (they depend on the lost frame): after a `refresh` a Host restarts decoding only at a frame with the key bit or the repair bit set, and drops the frames before it.
+- Prepare step: before its first frame the game builds the prewarm lists' pipelines and, when not done for this game version, the base of every shader pair (`DM_STREAM_PREPARE=0`: in the background while it plays instead). The hello comes first, at the connection; then a `prepare` message when a phase starts, at most 4 a second while it runs, and one with done equal to total when it ends (phase 2 ends when every pair is handed to a worker: a few compiles may still finish behind the game). A phase with nothing to do sends one message, 0 of 0; phase 2 is sent only when this start builds the pairs. No `video` or `audio` comes before the last `prepare`; the first `video` after it is a key frame. A `quit` meanwhile ends the process within 2 s: the pipeline archive keeps every file written so far, and the bases of the flush period under way are built again at the next start. While the game plays, the archive's timed write waits as in a window, until the game has presented no frame for ten seconds and no compile is under way (with `DM_STREAM_PREPARE=0` the background prewarm's own timed writes, every 60 s doubling up to 16 min, still go ahead) ([A timed archive write stalls active presentation](reference/rendering.md#a-timed-archive-write-stalls-active-presentation)).
+- The stream ends (the host exits gracefully) on `quit`, a closed socket, a read or write error, an unknown type, a bad length or a message of the wrong size.
+
 ## Following main
 
 nxnative has no releases or tags: a front end pins a commit and moves it forward. Between the commit it has (`A`) and the one it moves to (`B`), two things say what changed for it.
